act 19 DISCRIMINATION COMMIT: OL1, the shared structural theorem, which runs first

This is the first commit on this branch carrying a discriminating result, and
it is record 3 of the five the ordering obligation requires. The result that
crosses the boundary is named exactly: the proof of the shared structural
theorem OL1, in both of the forms the freeze fixes for it.

  ol1a_descends_to_composition -- OL1 (a), the general form. An L-PROP law
    that is quotient-well-defined (L4d, the first conjunct of TransitionLaw)
    and compositional descends to a composition of maps on the admissible
    orbit spaces. Four conjuncts: every E t is well defined on classes, so
    the evolution from the initial orbit is a function of the initial class
    alone; the solution set is read off the transition; every solution sits
    at the composite applied to its own initial slice; and the composite's
    own trajectories are solutions realized by a coherent lift. The composite
    E is a bound variable pinned by its two defining equations and is not a
    definition of this round.

  ol1b_monoid_action -- OL1 (b), the homogeneous form, at time-homogeneous
    visible families ONLY. The orbit space is then one set, the transition
    family is constant, E_0 is the identity and E_{t+s} = E_s . E_t, so the
    law is a monoid action of (N, +) on the admissible orbit space.

ACT 17's TJ1 IS CITED AT THE STEP, not in a footnote: it is conjunct 4 of
(a). Reading the solution set as a composition of maps on per-time state
spaces requires the ambient admissible set to be the product over time of
those spaces; intersecting a product constraint with a non-product ambient
set need not factor, and tj1_sufficiency is what makes the assembled
trajectory admissible. TJ1 is consumed at merged strength.

This is a DESCENT statement and not an existence statement: that an L-PROP
law exists is act 18's and is consumed here. It says nothing about
faithfulness, transitivity, freeness or any symmetry property, the action is
not claimed to be a group, and the transition is realized as no operator, no
unitary, no generator and no group element.

From this commit onward no rung statement and no frozen quotient may change.

Both results print only [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].
